1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,064
When I was a child, at my grandmother's

2
00:00:03,064 --> 00:00:06,343
house, mornings began with the smell of
coffee.

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:11,417
Emama spread fresh grass and set out the
jebena.

4
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:17,286
She washed the green beans slowly, by
hand.

5
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:24,525
As the beans roasted in the pan, the
smoke filled the whole house.

6
00:00:25,442 --> 00:00:32,111
But I was always in a hurry. "Emama,
when will it be ready?"

7
00:00:33,225 --> 00:00:36,328
She would smile and answer: "Slowly,

8
00:00:36,328 --> 00:00:40,034
slowly, an egg will walk on its own
legs."

9
00:00:40,942 --> 00:00:45,738
She pounded the beans in the mortar, and
the incense smoked.

10
00:00:46,650 --> 00:00:53,705
Abol, tona, bereka. Three rounds, three
lessons in patience.

11
00:00:54,608 --> 00:01:02,863
The neighbours gathered. News, laughter,
blessings. No one was in a hurry.

12
00:01:03,775 --> 00:01:08,751
Today I live in a faraway city.
Everything is fast.

13
00:01:09,775 --> 00:01:13,811
But when I roast coffee, I hear Emama's
voice.

14
00:01:16,575 --> 00:01:17,919
Slowly, slowly.
